  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In phonon-mediated high-entropy-alloy superconductors, Tc is primarily controlled by average valence electron count.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Atomic disorder is not the primary control on Tc in these alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9329343::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "[TaNb]0.31(TiZrHf)0.69 is a body-centered-cubic alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5740615::webcard",
        "PMC7070041::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "[TaNb]0.31(TiZrHf)0.69 has a random atomic distribution.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5740615::webcard",
        "PMC9329343::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The [TaNb]0.31(TiZrHf)0.69-type alloy is a phonon-mediated superconductor.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard",
        "PMC9329343::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The [TaNb]0.31(TiZrHf)0.69-type alloy is an isotropic s-wave superconductor in the dirty limit.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9329343::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing Zr with U or another element of different valence changes the alloy's average VEC.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr-to-U substitution can retain the BCC structure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr-to-U or analogous substitution can leave the overall level of structural disorder essentially unchanged.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Known superconducting HEAs of this family have Tc below approximately 10 K.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard",
        "PMC9329343::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant alloys follow a weak-coupling BCS regime.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9329343::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Maintaining a random multi-element BCC framework makes VEC the primary difference between the compared samples.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Average VEC determines the electronic density of states at the Fermi level.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The density of states at the Fermi level dictates electron-phonon coupling strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An optimal VEC maximizes electron-phonon coupling and thereby raises Tc.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Moving VEC away from its optimum lowers the density of states available for Cooper pairing and lowers Tc even at similar disorder.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Samples with an optimized, higher VEC will have a higher Tc than samples with lower or non-optimal VEC.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Observed Tc variations between x = 0.35 and x = 0.71 films in the (TaNb)1-x(ZrHfTi)x family cannot be explained by disorder effects.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9329343::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "[TaNb]0.31(TiUHf)0.69 is a BCC, phonon-mediated superconductor with Tc approximately 3.2 K.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7070041::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strong electronic correlations, substantial disorder changes, or non-phononic pairing could invalidate the proposed VEC control.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
